Version 1.14 (14 August 2026)

  * extend network data collector to support Pensando and Broadcom RoCE NIC
    families with throughput and fabric-health metrics (#307)
  * switch kernel tracing library from libcurl to header-only cpp-httplib (#308)
  * enable automatic code coverage reporting for data collectors (#309)
  * add warning when `perf_event_paranoid` setting is insufficient for hardware counter
    collection (#313)
  * improve `omnistat-query --export` performance for jobs with large numbers of short
    processes; adds separate process inventory CSV with per-process byte counts and
    timing (#314)
  * add GPU serial number as a label to `rocm_version_info` metric for inventory tracking (#315)

Version 1.13 (13 July 2026)

  * add skills support for agentic analysis to analyze Omnistat databases or exported CSV files (#271)
  * fix GPU kernel panels showing incorrect values for kernels with a single data point (#290)
  * improve process-based I/O monitoring in user-mode to avoid duplication (#291)
  * add ability to export host metrics (#292)
  * introduction of new optional data collector to support external (3rd party) metrics (#296)
  * add figure-of-merit discussion to documentation (#297, #298)
  * update rocmsmi-based collector to dynamically derive necessary C struct bindings from
    ROCm bindings file (#299)
  * add `rocm_energy_joules` metric for GPU energy accumulation tracking (#300)
  * add additional internal performance metric for user-mode data collection (#302)
  * update default SMI collector to use amd-smi variant (#303)
  * introduction of rack-level cluster dashboard generator for physical rack-layout
    visualization in Grafana (#304)

Version 1.12 (26 April 2026)

  * simplify kernel trace library finalization/flushing to avoid race condition (#276)
  * fix missing import in hardware counter collector (#277)
  * add CI coverage for hardware counter collection (#278)
  * update user-mode SSH startup to use pre-specified shell (#281)
  * add ROCm runtime version checks for kernel tracing compatibility (#282)
  * add `--localjob name` option to omnistat-usermode for single-node execution without a
    resource manager (#285)
  * add timing measurements for user-mode startup and teardown phases (#286)
  * add cache hit-rate counter definitions to runtime configuration and panels (#284, #288)

Version 1.11 (26 March 2026)

  * introduction of new optional data collector to support application-level kernel traces (#241)
  * performance refactoring for `pm_counter` (vendor counters) data collector  (#269)
  * modifications to default runtime configuration options (#270)
  * inclusion of FLOPS and HBM info in query CLI summary when present (#273)
  * adjustments to user-mode teardown process (#268, #275)

Version 1.10 (20 Februrary 2026)

  * updated loading mechanism for amd-smi python interface (#258)
  * fix for local NVMe I/O tracking observed on external system (#259)
  * introduction of new info and internal performance timing metrics (#263)  
  * various dashboard updates and fixes (#256, #264)
  * addition of optional network collector to enable more counters on Slingshot CXI
    interconnects - thanks to @gitrepoidoscar for the contribution (#260, #265)

Version 1.9 (09 December 2025)

  * enum bug fix for newer Python versions (#237)
  * expanded CI tests (#230, #239)    
  * introduction of new optional data collector to track host-oriented metrics (#242, #249, #251)
  * various dashboard updates and query outputs (#236, #250, #253)

Version 1.8 (19 September 2025)

  * added ability to control log level via environment variable (#215)
  * documentation updates to include vendor metrics (#217)
  * refactor of hardware counter sampling to leverage rocprofiler-sdk and support multiplexing (#221)
  * refactored collector base class to simplify dynamic loading and sharing of runtime configuration (#222)
  * updated python dependencies (#223, #224)
  * added support to track XGMI read/write traffic in SMI collectors (#226)

Version 1.7 (08 August 2025)

  * documentation enhancements outlining data collector options and available metrics (#175)
  * enhancement to `omnistat-query` to support filtering by annotation marker strings (#196)
  * Grafana dashboard improvements and additions for vendor energy metrics (#203)
  * introduction of new optional data collector to track decoder utilization (#204)
  * fix for CU occupancy collector when underlying file is missing (#207)
  * example kernel buffer collector added to contrib area of Omnistat to track the number and
   severity of `amdgpu` driver messages (#209). Contrib features are intended to house tech
   previews, experimental features that may not be fully supported in mainline Omnistat, or
   3rd-party contributions of general interest to the community.
  * Omnistat repository migrated to https://github.com/ROCm/omnistat

Version 1.6 (15 July 2025)

  * addition of new optional data collector to track CU occupancy (#178)
  * updated query tool to support shorter job executions and expand CI testing (#186)
  * dashboard reorganization and enhancements (#189)
  * addition of new optional data collector to track vendor-provided power/energy counters (#190)

Version 1.5.1 (18 June 2025)

  * update RAS block enumerations for newer Python versions (#179, #180)
  * updated RAS panels for Grafana (#182)
  * support API change of amdsmi in ROCM 6.4 (#183)
  * allow for override of push data frequency with `--pushinterval` (#184)

Version 1.5 (17 May 2025)

  * added job tracking support for the PBS resource manager (in addition to SLURM, Flux) (#162)
  * updated logic for GPU index detection (#164)
  * add user-mode capability to push data directly to external VictoriaMetrics instance (#166)
  * introduce network collector to gather transmit/receive rates on local network devices on a per-NIC
    basis - includes support for Slingshot CXI and InfiniBand high-speed interconnects (#167)
  * numerous dashboard enhancements and management improvements (#160, #161, #168)
  * add power-capping metrics and ability for applications to supply their own figure-of-merit during
    user-mode via a REST API (#169)
  * introduce embedded parallel-ssh utility to support user-mode data collection on wider range of
    production systems (#170)

Version 1.4 (19 Mar 2025)

  * include new metrics to track GPU RAS counters along with example dashboard updates (#158)

Version 1.3 (17 Feb 2025)

  * expand documentation to include developer's guide (#155)
  * add startup check for valid numa core binding (#153)
  * allow override of numactl process binding settings via environment variables (#151)
  * add support for combining multiple user-mode data collections (#149)

Version 1.2 (17 Jan 2025)

  * update VictoriaMetric server endpoint check in user-mode (#147)
  * tweak Flask endpoint return to use `text/plain` content type (#146)
  * extend `omnistat-query` to support exporting of CSV time series data (#145)
  * avoid data collector stoppage when SLURM squeue times out (#142)
  * expand error message when loading omnistat modules (#141)

Version 1.1 (07 Jan 2025)

  * updated standalone user-mode data collection to support a "push" model using VictoriaMetrics (#133)
  * added user-mode support for the Flux resource manager (in addition to SLURM) (#132, #133, #135)
  * updated query utility to support Flux-style jobids (#136)

Version 1.0 (07 Oct 2024)

  * initial Omnistat release
